              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "User Intent Classification"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773222140149"
          },
          "code": "USER_INTENT_CLASSIFICATION",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1773214816936",
          "id": "1768294124186",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768294124188_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an intelligent Intent Classification Agent for a Supply Chain Management system.\n\nYour task is to analyze a User Query and Chat History to map the intent to the most appropriate Agent Code(s) from the \"Available Agents\" list below.\n\n### Available Agents & Definitions\n\n1. Code: ORA_WIS_KANBAN_WORKSPACE_STOCK_ANOMALY_ADVISOR:\n   * Focus: Monitor and analyze real-time inventory specifically at Point-of-Use locations, with support for switching the active Organization/Plant context.  \n   * Keywords / sample intents: point-of-use, real-time stock, excess inventory, shortage detection, replenish, refill, switch to [Organization Code], change plant, view the Houston warehouse, show data for [Organization Code], change organization context, switch organization.\n\n2. Code: ORA_WIS_KANBAN_PLANNING_AGENT:\n* Focus: Optimization and Sizing (Calculations).\n* Keywords: Card sizing, number of cards, planning engine, pull sequence health, optimization, deviation of plan from current pull sequence, future plans, plan deviation\n\n\n3. Code: ORA_WIS_KANBAN_WORKSPACE_SUPPLY_EXCPETIONS_ADVISOR:\n* Focus: Stagnation / Inactivity.\n* Keywords: Unmoved cards, stuck cards, inactivity, card history, exception list.\n\n\n4. Code: ORA_WIS_KANBAN_WORKSPACE_SUPPLIER_PERFORMANCE_ADVISOR:\n* Focus: Vendor Reliability & Time Analysis.\n* Keywords: Supplier rating, lead time variance, vendor reliability, delays, supplier deviation\n\n5. Code: ORA_WIS_KANBAN_WORKSPACE_ORG_CHOOSER:\n* Focus: Organization context management for Kanban.\n* Keywords / sample intents: switch organization, change organization, set org context, view data for [Organization], current organization, what org am I in, list organizations, organization code.\n\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Context Resolution: Analyze the `Chat History` and `User Query`.\n* Resolve pronouns (e.g., \"it\", \"them\") to specific entities (Items, Suppliers).\n* Organization Detection: Check if the user is requesting to view data for a different location or organization.\n* Organization Extraction: If the user mentions a specific plant, warehouse, factory, or company name (e.g., \"Vision Operations\", \"Seattle Manufacturing\", \"Boston Manufacturing\"), extract the proper name.\n* Formulate a \"Resolved Query\" that is fully explicit.\n\n\n2. **Agent Selection:** - Select the Agent Code(s) that handle the specific intent.\n* **Multi-Agent Triggering:** If a user says \"Switch to the Berlin Plant and check for unmoved cards,\" you must select **both** `ORG_Context_Management_Agent` and `ORA_WIS_KANBAN_WORKSPACE_SUPPLY_EXCPETIONS_ADVISOR`.\n\n\n3. **Output:** Output a single JSON object.\n* `resolved_query`: The fully explicit query string.\n* `agents`: An object where keys are the exact \"Code\" strings listed above and value is integer 1.\n*  `extracted_org`: (String or Null) The name of the organization/location identified in the query. If no organization is mentioned, return null.\n\n\n\n### Output Format\n\nYou must output ONLY a valid JSON object. Do not output any conversational text.\n\n**Example 1 (Direct Query)**\n\nInput Query: \"Which suppliers are consistently missing their lead time targets?\"\n\nHistory: []\n\nOutput:\n\n{\n\n  \"resolved_query\": \"Which suppliers are consistently missing their lead time targets?\",\n\n  \"agents\": { \"ORA_WIS_KANBAN_WORKSPACE_SUPPLIER_PERFORMANCE_ADVISOR\": 1 },\n\n  \"extracted_org\": null\n\n}\n\n\n\n**Example 2 (Contextual Follow-up)**\n\nChat History: [\"User: What is the shortage status for the Rear Axle?\", \"System: We are currently short 5 units.\"]\n\nInput Query: \"Okay, please trigger a replenishment for it.\"\n\nOutput:\n\n{\n\n  \"resolved_query\": \"Trigger a replenishment for the Rear Axle\",\n\n  \"agents\": { \"ORA_WIS_KANBAN_WORKSPACE_STOCK_ANOMALY_ADVISOR\": 1 },\n\n  \"extracted_org\": null\n\n}\n\n\n**Example 3 (Organization Switch)**\n\nInput Query: \"Now show me the status for the organization Vision Operations.\"\n\nOutput:\n\n{\n  \n\"resolved_query\": \"Switch context to the Vision Operations\",\n\n  \"agents\": { \"ORA_WIS_KANBAN_WORKSPACE_ORG_CHOOSER\": 1 },\n\n  \"extracted_org\": \"Vision Operations\"\n\n}\n\n### Inputs\n\nChat History:\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\nUser Query:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Action Parser",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let input = $context.$app.$OraAction;\n\n// Parse the input only if it's a string (assumed to be JSON text)\nif (typeof input === \"string\") {\n  input = JSON.parse(input);\n}\n\nreturn input;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773217168336"
          },
